+# ARM emit-loop counter-pointer investigation (2026-10-25)
+
+Tags: #matching #compiler #iwram
+
+Investigated 08000430 in `src/iwram_code.c` from the supplied exact pinned
+baseline, working solo. No new exact match or coverage gain. The best unpinned
+source remains the prior four-instruction near-match; its residue is the cursor
+address load appearing late in each emit-loop preheader.
+
+The local research record is `build/arm_kit/REPORT.md`: 83 default/diagnostic
+runs, candidate sources, pass dumps and compiler priority logs. Retained local
+sources include direct counter globals (8 instruction differences), the
+palette-loop pointer-copy route (18), and a natural request helper without the
+b/b2 dead initializers (71). Knob-only zero-diff outputs are diagnostics, not
+accepted matches.
+
+Direct globals plus diagnostic sched1 load reclassification on the two cursor
+preheader sets removes the emit residue. A separate collect-loop priority tie
+accounts for the remaining four differences; changing both decisions yields
+zero instruction diffs. The palette-copy route instead preserves the test
+reload and preheader copy but loses cse2 constant notes at the palette exit,
+raising the pointer's allocation priority. Simple early aliases let GCSE PRE
+remove the test reloads. Detailed UIDs and pseudo numbers are in the report
+and apply only to its captured source.
+
+Boktai 2 has the same sl cursor hoist, fresh r2 address load for the reservation
+test, signed attr2 read, and halfword increment. Its request writer differs in
+address construction and count reloads. Its Video_AllocObjTiles C favors direct
+global cursor expressions. Reconstructing the original inline API and its
+argument lifetimes from neighboring routines is the strongest next direction.
+
+Restored the supplied pinned baseline to `src/iwram_code.c` at closeout.
+`tools/check.py src/iwram_code.c`: all six functions MATCH, zero differing
+bytes across the 4364-byte unit including pools. No full build, commit or push.
